The optional Elephant-1 adapter implements Base Labs at Baseten's published
block-bidirectional attention and slot-LM readout. Its checkpoint is marked MIT.
Base Labs' chat_template.jinja supplies the role, image and generation markers.
Its serve.patch adds the block layout and readout used in training and serving.
The publisher pins OmniJev/OneJev (Apache-2.0) for the inherited qev-labels-v2
system and question wording, default option descriptions and slot order.
ANERun renders that format in Swift with the installed tokenizer and slot table.
Conversion and inference require no OneJev installation.
OneJev attributes the choice and score confidence formulas to TypeSafe AI
(MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 TypeSafe AI).
